  "context": "Implemented post-load per-table ANALYZE in PR #4058. Real 4GiB SingleStore stack: SF0.01 TPC-DS load,power completed all 103 queries in all three iterations (79.32s/98.27s/70.07s), including 24a; /tmp/obt/s5/run.log. No 24a pruning needed. JoinOrder SF1 ANALYZE retry /tmp/obt/s6/run.log hit 3000s bound while still Loading benchmark data, before power; cannot conclude ANALYZE fixes q7c, existing documented prune retained. Both stacks cleaned: container ls -a and mocker ps -a contain no SingleStore containers.",
  "description": "From the load-value-integrity batch (#4043). TPC-DS now loads on SingleStore, but the power phase at SF0.01 fails at query 24a with an out-of-memory error on the 4 GiB local stack. joinorder SF1 was pruned with a documented reason: memsqld is OOM-killed on query 7c.\n\nChange. Determine whether this is the stack's memory limit (compare against the release UAT runner's memory) or a query-plan problem on SingleStore. Then either size the UAT stack, or fix or prune the query with a recorded reason.\n\nGuardrails: work in a linked worktree; local stacks via make uat-bring-up under mocker, one at a time; no live cloud.",
